From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Wed, 17 Jun 2026 15:17:09 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 02365/11362] [outer-loop] tn36: mapped ALL buttons (6-bit
 editor) + solved L2 (16->17 levels)

Operator: 'map tn36's up/scale/rotate buttons and solve the next level.' DONE.

THE FULL TOOL PALETTE: each program slot is a 6-BIT code editor. Bit b's toggle-
button is at (slot_x, slot_y_top + 3*b) for b=0..5 (values 1,2,4,8,16,32), so ANY
command code = sum of its set bits: down(3)=bit0+bit1, UP(33)=bit0+bit5, SCALE+(8)=
bit3, ROTATE+90(5)=bit0+bit2, etc. So up/scale/rotate are all mapped. Slot positions
are READABLE from internal state (controller.pfyayhyovw[i].{x,y}) and re-lay-out per
level (L1: 5 slots, L2: 4 slots, different x/y) -> the solver DISCOVERS them.

L2 SOLVED: object (45,24)->target (45,8), dy=-16 = 4 ups. Set all 4 slots to code 33
(up) via bit0+bit5 -> [33,33,33,33] -> y:24->8 = win. Level 2 reached.

GENERAL SOLVER (scripts/arc3_tn36_offline_solver.py rewritten): reads deltas + the
per-level layout, computes the move-program (down/up/left/right + scale/rotate),
edits slots via bit-toggle clicks, runs, and CHAINS levels. Reproduces L1+L2
(reproduced=True claimed_level=2, 25 clicks). Registry: tn36 levels_reproduced 1->2,
reproducible_total 16->17. Only property-change (codes 14/15/63) remains undecoded.
